WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:09.139
Jon Heder shot to fame with the 2004 indie
hit Napoleon Dynamite. Now just a few years

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:14.769
later, he pretty much disappeared from the
spotlight, and these days, it seems like movie

00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:21.099
studios want nothing to do with him. Why isn't
Jon Heder welcome in Tinseltown anymore?

00:00:21.099 --> 00:00:23.999
“What do you want to do today Napoleon?”

00:00:23.999 --> 00:00:26.939
“Whatever I feel like I wanna do, gosh.”

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:27.779
One-hit wonder

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:33.280
This isn't to say that Jon Heder is a bad
actor. He's made some enjoyable films. It's

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.960
just that no matter what he does, he's never
going to shake Napoleon Dynamite. In School

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.650
for Scoundrels, he attempted to play a romantic
lead. In Blades of Glory, he played an eccentric,

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:50.030
disgraced figure skater. Yet whenever audiences
hear or see his name, they expect to see the

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:55.020
curly-haired, bespectacled nerd who danced
his way into movie watchers' hearts.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.820
A string of flops

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:03.050
Again, Heder has made some good flicks. Just
Like Heaven and Monster House both found financial

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:08.780
success, critical praise, or some combination
of the two. But if you look at his filmography,

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:13.659
those are the exceptions to the rule. Most
of his films, like Mama's Boy or Bling, were

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:20.420
greeted with critical wrath or outright indifference.
Even worse, most of his later films have made

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:27.539
very little money. Whether or not that's Heder's
fault, his name's attached to those projects.

00:01:27.539 --> 00:01:28.649
Not that nerdy

00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:33.789
Take away the hair, the glasses, and the "Vote
for Pedro" T-shirt, and Heder looks nothing

00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:39.729
like the awkward-but-heroic nerd fans took
him for in Napoleon Dynamite. In real life,

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:44.869
Heder resembles a classic, rugged leading
man with a five o'clock shadow, square chin,

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:50.399
and sharp jawline. Perhaps when the geek masses
saw the true Heder, they felt betrayed and

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:52.799
turned their backs on him.

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:55.279
“Frikin idiot”

00:01:55.279 --> 00:01:56.049
Voiceover work

00:01:56.049 --> 00:02:00.349
Even though we haven't seen that much of Jon
Heder lately, it doesn't mean he's out of

00:02:00.349 --> 00:02:06.499
the picture. In fact, he's been behind it.
Beginning with 2005's Monster House, Heder

00:02:06.499 --> 00:02:11.080
has booked a lot of voice work for video games,
animated films, and cartoons.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.340
“What the flip phone are you doing?”

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:17.530
“I was just helping out little pickle, he
has trouble breaking down the kernel with

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.220
his tiny little beak.”

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:24.820
He’s also lent his voice to an animated
series based on Napoleon Dynamite. To date,

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:30.330
he's had almost 20 voice credits, and the
work seems to be ramping up. It's not surprising,

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.390
considering his distinctive voice.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.630
“Hi Randy, delivering the papers again?”

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:42.480
“Yes, you don’t have to ask the same question
every day.”

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.770
So it could be a matter of him not wanting
to bother with Hollywood anymore. Which brings

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.960
us to his other venture…

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:49.560
On the web

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:54.900
While his prolific voiceover career keeps
him busy, Heder hasn't completely retreated

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.990
from the camera. Like many creative professionals,
he's gone to work for himself by taking his

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:06.220
talents to the internet. Since 2009, Heder's
appeared in web-exclusive programs, like the

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:11.580
zombie comedy Woke Up Dead. With these successful
online ventures and the creative freedom that

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:16.710
they offer, there's no reason for him to bother
with Hollywood productions. He's already got

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.900
all the opportunity he needs.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.720
Uncontroversial

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:26.190
Jon Heder leads a fairly innocent life. The
reason movie watchers are attracted to some

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:32.610
celebs is that they're human trainwrecks.
Or film fans clamor for a star who's overcome

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:39.040
a serious, debilitating problem. Either way,
Hollywood loves a good controversy. After

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.690
all, there's no such thing as bad publicity.
Heder's never had any problems like that.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:49.540
Nothing sensational ever really occurred in
his public life. In fact, he's even made sure

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:55.140
to stay away from potential projects because
they conflicted with his Mormon faith, and

00:03:55.140 --> 00:04:00.120
he believed they'd attract the wrong kind
of attention. He might be so squeaky clean

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.710
that there's nothing for gawking ticket buyers
to stick to.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.630
What's next

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:09.670
Jon Heder could revive his career pretty easily,
and he doesn't have to compromise his values

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:13.780
to do it. And seeing as how he's worked on
multiple platforms, it's pretty much up to

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.109
him how he gets his productions to the people.

00:04:16.109 --> 00:04:24.590
“Yeah, to mermaid pools filled with puppies
drool and centaurs pulling candy sleigh.”

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:29.760
Or, if nothing like that pans out, he could
always take after Kip and train to become

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.790
a cage fighter.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.560
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:40.180
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which Jon Heder roles have been your

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:40.800
favorite...

